# solar-ctl SSH policy: root-only, key-only.
#
# "-s" disables password logins -> only holders of a key in
# /root/.ssh/authorized_keys (installed by the solar-rootkeys recipe) get
# in, and only as root: every other account has no key and no usable
# password. OE's default "-w" would deny root logins entirely.
#
# NOTE: the allow-root-login IMAGE_FEATURE's postcommand seds away "-w"
# lines here (ours ships neither). NEVER use "-B" for this: dropbear's -B
# means "allow blank password logins", not "reject passwords" -- combined
# with the lab empty-root-password feature, pre-2025 dropbear versions
# would then let anyone in as root with an empty password. dropbear
# 2025.89 happens to reject blank passwords anyway, but -s is the
# correct, explicit way to switch password auth off.
DROPBEAR_EXTRA_ARGS="-s"
